ion  anything  ongoing because that is a case where  the creators become aware of the  audience aware of the audience's  expectations  aware of what the audience hopes to see  and can start  deliberately toying and messing with  them and  baiting them most of the more egregious  examples where i think there is  actually tangible evidence that the  creators knew fully well what they were  doing  and did it anyway and it just comes off  as kind of mean  are things like bbc sherlock  supernatural  even the the film series that i can  think of that people have accused of  queerbaiting are things that have been  around for a long time  long enough for their fans to have built  expectations things like  star wars or the mcu even if you're  gonna make those arguments  i still feel like queerbaiting is  something that happens to something that  goes on for a long time  happening in a one-off film it's  pretty uncommon and  my own personal experience viewing the  film i came away thinking  i was so happy at how wholesome the  relationship between these two boys was  and i should clarify when i say  wholesome i don't mean not sexual i mean  wholesome as in  not toxic because so often  depictions of relationships between  young boys  even platonic ones contain a lot of  toxic elements there's so often this  competitiveness this one upsmanship  this desire to be better or this  sort of sense of jealousy or whatever  and none of that's here  it's just a wonderful bonding  relationship  between these two and i was just happy  to see that because  i feel like i don't see that very much  i feel like i don't see this kind of  close-knit  wholesome and stable relationship  between two male characters who aren't  like siblings who aren't brothers or  something  it's really rare and i was just happy to  see that  now i can again concede that  if i had been hoping for and waiting for  seeing two male characters in a disney  movie be confirmed as a couple  then yeah i probably would have thought  it's just nice to see that  too i personally didn't really see it  in lucca but again i wasn't tapped into  the conversations that were going on  ahead of time  and while i've seen some you know cases  made  it comes back to a large part of the  reason why i generally don't talk about  queer baiting  in the broadest sense because  it kind of depends on interpreting the  intention of the creators  and that's much easier to do in  something like a show  or something that is long running  because you can look at patterns  patterns will absolutely reveal more  about intentionality  one-off films  oftentimes it can really involve a heck  of a lot more armchair psychology and  trying to  just parse the thought process of  creators and  companies then i'm frankly comfortable  doing when it comes to creative works  like this  were those kinds of things in their  heads they say they weren't  could they be lying yeah but then we're  getting into the kind of conspiratorial  narrative that  i'm just not comfortable doing i will  say this  if we ever find out a later date from  someone behind the scenes of  luca at pixar that they very much wanted  to make this a queer story but were shut  down  by people higher up either within pixar  or disney if that ever comes out oh yeah  i'm gonna  talk about that like you wouldn't  believe  but without that i'm not  seeing this as at least not the  strongest  incidence of queerbaiting i'm not going  to say definitively that it's not  because i don't want to invalidate  people's feelings and like i said  i'm not quite as dialed into all this as  i know some people  are so i'm not trying to shut anybody  down if they did come away from this  film feeling like they were baited  but i i do feel comfortable saying it's  not the strongest case  for this kind of thing and that's where  i land  on all of this what do you think about  it have you seen luca  did you get these vibes from it were you  pleasantly surprised to get these vibes  were you frustrated by these vibes  whatever your thoughts are what do you  think about queerbaiting in general  what are your most egregious examples  whatever your thoughts are politely  leave them down in the comments and  let's talk about it  usual stuff like share subscribe i have  a patreon that is how i pay my bills  keeps this whole operation up and  running but you don't have to do that  there are rewards for every tier but  there's also youtube memberships but  even if you don't want to do that  the other stuff i mentioned helps me out  as well  but you don't have to do any of it  because what i really want you to  remember is that you are beautiful  you are valid and you are loved  you are the council i'm just running the  meetings  and until next time this council is  adjourned  hope you have a good rest of pride  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  you um  [Music]

